/**
 * @file ggsw_ciphertext.dox
 * @brief Documentation of the bivGGSW ciphertext representation.
 *
 * @page ggsw_ciphertext bivGGSW Ciphertext
 *
 * ## Overview
 *
 * A bivGGSW ciphertext encodes a small integer polynomial represented by a function \(f\).
 *
 * The ciphertext is represented as a matrix of size
 * \[
 * n_{\text{limbs\_tilde}} \times n_{\text{limbs}}
 * \]
 * with coefficients in 
 * \[
 * \mathbb{Z}_n[X]
 * \].
 *
 * Each row \(i\) is a bivGLWE ciphertext encrypting \(f(H(i))\).
 *
 * Matrix representation:
 * \[
 * \begin{bmatrix}
 * \text{GLWE}(f(H(0))) \\
 * \vdots \\
 * \text{GLWE}(f(H(n_{\text{limbs\_tilde}} - 1)))
 * \end{bmatrix}
 * \]
 *
 * ## Gadget matrix
 *
 * The gadget matrix \(H\) is built using the gadget base
 * \[
 * (2^kappa) = 2^{\tilde{\kappa}}
 * \].
 *
 * It is reorganized in powers of \((2^kappa)\) to preserve the prefix property.
 *
 * Matrix blocks:
 * \[
 * \begin{bmatrix}
 * 1/(2^kappa) & 0 & 0 & \dots & 0 \\
 * 0 & 1/(2^kappa) & 0 & \dots & 0 \\
 * \vdots & \vdots & \vdots & & \vdots \\
 * 0 & 0 & 0 & \dots & 1/(2^kappa)
 * \end{bmatrix},
 * \quad
 * \begin{bmatrix}
 * 1/(2^kappa)^2 & 0 & 0 & \dots & 0 \\
 * 0 & 1/(2^kappa)^2 & 0 & \dots & 0 \\
 * \vdots & \vdots & \vdots & & \vdots \\
 * 0 & 0 & 0 & \dots & 1/(2^kappa)^2
 * \end{bmatrix},
 * \dots
 * \]
 *
 * Each block corresponds to one power of the gadget base.
 *
 * ## GLWEGadget ciphertext (OUT-OF-DATE)
 *
 * A GLWEGadget ciphertext is obtained by
 * restricting the full bivGGSW ciphertext to a subset of rows corresponding
 * to a fixed power of the gadget base \((2^kappa)\).
 *
 * For a given gadget level \(j\), the partial bivGGSW is the submatrix of the bivGGSW ciphertext that encrypts the polynomial \(f\) multiplied
 * by the gadget vector entries associated with \(1 / (2^kappa)^j\).
 *
 * In terms of the gadget matrix \(H\), a partial bivGGSW corresponds to one
 * block of \(n_\text{limbs}\) consecutive rows:
 * \[
 * \begin{bmatrix}
 * 1/(2^kappa)^j & 0 & 0 & \dots & 0 \\
 * 0 & 1/(2^kappa)^j & 0 & \dots & 0 \\
 * \vdots & \vdots & \vdots & & \vdots \\
 * 0 & 0 & 0 & \dots & 1/(2^kappa)^j
 * \end{bmatrix}
 * \]
 *
 * Each row of this block is a bivGLWE ciphertext encrypting \(f\) multiplied
 * by the corresponding gadget coefficient.
 *
 * A full bivGGSW ciphertext is the vertical concatenation of all partial bivGGSW ciphertexts
 * for \(j = 1, \dots, \tilde{l}\).
 */
